member.summary:
Resolves the community/actor's feed collection IRI by capability. The client reads the document's own advertised endpoints and the server it talks to, in priority order:
the iris:feed extension, when the server advertises it (an Iris instance — its feed endpoint, which also supports the ?q= content-search the community feed search relies on);
otherwise, for a Lemmy community, {actor}/outbox — Lemmy has no /feed endpoint; a community's posts are the Create/Announce activities in its outbox (rendered by the client's content-object view, which unwraps the activity's object);
otherwise, {actor}/feed — the Mastodon/Pleroma convention for a followed feed.
The single, capability-aware read a UI uses to point its feed collection at the right route for whatever server the community lives on (137.2).
